Notes:

1- castor-norm needs a datafile with all possible lines of response. This means even if in practice we cannot have a line of response we need to have an entry with 0 for the detected values. So, for example if castorID1 and castorID2 are in the same block (in a plain) and say castorID2 = castorID1++ then we need to have a record/event line with histData[castorID1, castorID2] = 0. However, for a datafile to be reconstructed, it does not need to contain these inpossible lines. I have reconstructed phantoms without having these impossible lines and my histogram mode datafile only contained recored lines and I was able to recontruct my point sources. i did not have normalization at all. To conclude, castor-norm needs all lines of responses (they are theoretically possible but practically inpossible.)
